# Dependencies and build output
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
.DS_Store

# Environment.
# .env.example IS tracked on purpose — it documents the contact-form variables
# without carrying any values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COMMENTS MUST BE ON THEIR OWN LINE.
#
# Git does not support trailing comments. A line written as
#
#     source-video/          # 28 MB of source MP4
#
# is read as a LITERAL pattern including the spaces and the comment text, so it
# matches nothing at all. That is exactly how this file used to be written, and
# it meant `source-video/` was never ignored — 28 MB of MP4 would have gone into
# the first commit and stayed in history permanently. Confirmed with
# `git check-ignore -v`, which reported the path as not ignored.
#
# If you add an entry here, put any explanation on the line above it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Heavy local-only inputs. The WebP frames in public/ are the shipped artefact;
# these are the raw material they were cut from, plus the superseded originals.
source-video/
_old-ezgif-frames/

# Source logo artwork (~2 MB of JPG). The site draws the mark as inline SVG in
# ConvexMark.jsx, so nothing in the build reads these.
assets-convex-funding-logo/

# Design references kept on disk but never shipped or pushed — currently the type
# specimen the Archivo decision was made from.
_design/

# Local AI tooling. None of it is needed to build, run or deploy the site.
# NOTE: .claude/launch.json is deliberately NOT ignored — it is the dev-server
# config and belongs in the repo.
.agents/
.claude/skills/
skills-lock.json

# Local handoff notes. Ignored rather than deleted: they are the only record of
# the measured architecture decisions behind this build.
PROJECT-STATE.md
HANDOFF-NEXT-SESSION.md

# Local Cloudflare/Wrangler emulator state, created by `wrangler pages dev`.
# Regenerated on demand; nothing here belongs in the repo.
.wrangler/
